// RUN: onnx-mlir-opt --recompose-onnx --constprop-onnx --canonicalize --mlir-elide-elementsattrs-if-larger=16 %s -split-input-file | FileCheck %s

// GROUND-ALL: -r="--disable-split-matmul-by-slice"

// The constant weight of every test is the same 2x768 tensor, with values
// ((37*col + 11*row) % 17 - 8) / 8: not a splat, so that slicing it at the
// wrong offset changes the results grounding compares. CHECK lines elide the
// constants and pin the structure; grounding pins the values.

// Gated MLP (SwiGLU-style): one MatMul against a constant weight, whose output
// is split in two halves along the last axis by two Slices. The Slices move
// onto the constant weight and are folded away, leaving two narrower MatMuls
// and no Slice.
// GROUND-THIS: --shape-info=0:2x3x2
func.func @test_split_matmul_by_slice(%arg0: tensor<?x?x2xf32> {onnx.name = "x"}) -> (tensor<?x?x384xf32> {onnx.name = "y"}) {
